process-teams.m's seventeen adders spawned on the machine's GPU: they fill
more slots than one team of the kernel has, and every one answers, as all
the kernel's teams run (docs/INPROGRESS.md, GPU processes without omp
target, step 4b).
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-teams.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env %t2 | FileCheck %S/process-teams.m --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace

A kernel whose code recurses has a stack that is not fixed, of the size its
launch gives, 1536 bytes a lane, whose scratch the GPU holds for every
team.
RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/Inputs/process_teams_recursive.m -o %t.recursive
RUN: %gpu-env %t.recursive | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FIB
FIB: 6765

With the plugin's own size, 16 KiB, the GPU does not hold the scratch of
every team, and those it holds back would never start. The spawn that
launches the kernel waits for them, and reports it.
RUN: not %gpu-env MERK_GPU_PROCESS_STACK_BYTES=16384 MERK_TEAMS_STALL_MILLISECONDS=1000 %t.recursive 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HELD
HELD: Software Error: process.spawn: GPU 0 started {{[0-9]+}} of the {{[0-9]+}} teams of the module process_teams_recursive's processes' kernel, which must all run at once, and no other within 1000 ms (MERK_TEAMS_STALL_MILLISECONDS): the GPU may not hold their scratch for all of them, as for a kernel with a dynamic stack

RUN: not %gpu-env MERK_GPU_PROCESS_STACK_BYTES=1k %t.recursive 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BAD
BAD: Software Error: process.spawn: MERK_GPU_PROCESS_STACK_BYTES is not a positive number of bytes: 1k

A recursion deeper than the stack has room for ends the program, rather
than overflow it: the procedure checks the stack at its entry against the
limit that the runtime set. A shallow one runs.
RUN: not %gpu-env %t.recursive deep 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DEEP
DEEP: Mercury runtime: stack overflow in a GPU process: MERK_GPU_PROCESS_STACK_BYTES gives GPU processes more stack
RUN: %gpu-env %t.recursive shallow | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SHALLOW
SHALLOW: 121

A stack smaller than what the kernel's calls take outside the recursion
cannot run it: the spawn that loads the image says so.
RUN: not %gpu-env MERK_GPU_PROCESS_STACK_BYTES=64 %t.recursive 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FRAMES
FRAMES: Software Error: process.spawn: the module process_teams_recursive's processes take {{[0-9]+}} bytes of stack a lane for their calls on GPU 0, and GPU processes have 64: a larger MERK_GPU_PROCESS_STACK_BYTES gives them more, which may keep some of their kernel's teams from starting
